# `target/` — trailing slash, unanchored. Matches a build directory at any depth
# (which the spike workspace needs) without also ignoring a *file* named `target`,
# which `**/target` would silently do.
target/

# Spike artefacts. `spike.db` is regenerated by setup-db.py on every run, and the
# lockfile is left out on purpose: a spike asks whether the design still holds
# against a current dependency, so resolving fresh is what makes a divergence
# surface. See spikes/*/README.md.
spikes/**/spike.db
spikes/**/Cargo.lock

# Spec private docs
docs/ 

